 #uuid "62b01f1f-915d-551f-87fc-c511ebf0a88a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071277 #edb/ref 1080 "33^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071277 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071277 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9268c8c6-7552-55f4-be86-6e1e59c3e62b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071278 #edb/ref 1080 "34^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071278 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071278 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a1f35c23-f7f5-51c0-8019-7b3098ba8ac0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071279 #edb/ref 1080 "32^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071279 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071279 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b64a613a-0e7d-56da-9bb4-82318ed4de6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071280 #edb/ref 1080 "29^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071280 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071280 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d87fd8a9-909f-50db-bb23-655299660d9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071281 #edb/ref 1080 "30^{∘}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071281 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186071281 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "071decc7-c4d2-5be8-8973-c39af8a5736b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073507 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14725" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073507 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1a/1afba9a36c6fd04fecfd50877181380776e13a83422697de4a39d71381f09aff.png)\n\nFind the value of $x$ in the triangle above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073507 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed0361cf-cec0-5ec2-baab-e0f558619191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073507 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the sum of the measures of the interior angles in any triangle is equal to $180^\\circ$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠A + m∠B + m∠C &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n36^{∘} + 112^{∘} + x &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n148^{∘} + x &= 180^{∘} \\\\\nx &= 32^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073508 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14727" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073508 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e4/e43daa39b169c8ba29c21dd33e7a7fab1e92c7c78eafbd1021971e1883f6c9f8.png)\n\nFind the measure of $\\angle C$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073508 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf72c879-105c-5416-8dbd-7976228f0b4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073508 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is $180^\\circ$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3z + 4z + 40^{∘} &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n7z + 40^{∘} &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n7z &= 140^{∘} \\\\\nz &= 20^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠C &= 4z \\\\\n&= 4(20^{∘}) \\\\\n&= 80^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073509 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14728" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073509 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a triangle $\\triangle ABC$, where $m\\angle{A} = 55^\\circ$, $m\\angle B = x + 10^\\circ$, and $m\\angle C = 3x - 5^\\circ$. Find the value of $x$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073509 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8200fc85-afcc-5fb9-b942-cedbc87c739b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073509 #edb/ref 1074 "The sum of the measures of the interior angles must be $180^\\circ$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n55^{∘} + (x + 10^{∘}) + (3x - 5^{∘}) &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n60^{∘} + 4x &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n4x &= 120^{∘} \\\\\nx &= 30^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073510 #edb/ref 1069 "e-15572" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073510 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1a/1a24187f280eb99640c3d1bfae3b7fe873383f04c2c492e7873a40de16a9560b.png)\n\nFind the measure of angle $C$ given that $m\\angle{A} = m\\angle{B}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073510 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b015f8d6-ac1b-537d-a673-839fc7418f71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073510 #edb/ref 1074 "Using\n\n$$\nm\\angle{A} = m\\angle{B}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠A &= m∠B \\\\\n3x - 27^{∘} &= 2x \\\\\nx &= 27^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, substituting $x=27^\\circ$ in the expression for $m\\angle B$, we get\n\n$$\nm\\angle{B}=2(27^\\circ)=54^\\circ\n$$\n\nNow, we can find $m\\angle C$ using the fact that the internal angles of any triangle sum to $180^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm∠A + m∠B + m∠C &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n2m∠B + m∠C &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n2 \\cdot 54^{∘} + m∠C &= 180^{∘} \\\\\n108^{∘} + m∠C &= 180^{∘} \\\\\nm∠C &= 72^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073741 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073741 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073741 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073741 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073741 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Missing Angle in a Triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073741 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073741 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "fdb1e0fe-da89-5d80-b9a0-82d4daddc396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073742 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073742 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073742 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073742 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Unknown Quantity From a Triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073742 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073742 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3eb85b52-cd40-5469-b2f5-ceee2f0bf0cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073743 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073743 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Unknown Quantity Given a Description of a Triangle" #edb/re